        "id": 1892347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-18T13:04:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, that would correspond to `to_parent` rather than `from_parent`. We already have a `from_parent` field, though it\u0027s called `stack_next` for some reason.\n\nI\u0027m uploading a new version with this field renamed to `from_parent`.",
      "parentUuid": "f8159849_531b3ff0",
      "revId": "0dfd18dc7d1428993739d87d1ab015e8424b4393",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a780b557_8396e020",
        "filename": "drivers/android/thread.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 163,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-18T23:43:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right. I was thinking this was the rust version of binder_pop_transaction_ilocked which pops the transaction of the thread you are replying to, but pop_transaction_replied does that (with from_parent hidden in clone_next).\n\nI\u0027m guessing the rust version renamed `from_parent` to `stack_next` since `from_parent` must also be the next entry of the overall transaction stack. We don\u0027t have a pointer to the top of the transaction stack though, so we always need to update the current_transaction for both threads. The C version has both from_parent and to_parent and both of them are used when sending a reply. Can you have both of them in the rust version as well, so we don\u0027t need a search here?",
      "parentUuid": "6a4fa3c0_9ecefcd5",
      "revId": "0dfd18dc7d1428993739d87d1ab015e8424b4393",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b69ee1c_f926f58b",
        "filename": "drivers/android/thread.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 163,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-19T02:41:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "An example if it helps. Transactions are from thread on left to thread on right of the transaction line.\n```\nCurrent transaction:\n A               i    j  k        m  n        p\n B                i  j    k  l            o  p\n C                            l  m\n D                                    n  o\nThread:        A   B   A   B   C   A   D   B   A\nTransaction:     i   j   k   l   m   n   o   p\n from_parent:    -   i   j   k   l   m   n   o\n to_parent:      -   i   j   -   k   -   l   n\n```\nThere could be mistakes here, but you can see that from_parent looks like the transaction stack itself, while to_parent has gaps. To loop over all the transactions a single thread is involved in you alternate between to_parent and from_parent.",
      "parentUuid": "a780b557_8396e020",
      "revId": "0dfd18dc7d1428993739d87d1ab015e8424b4393",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8a71f6e_57f2df50",
        "filename": "drivers/android/thread.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 163,
      "author": {
        "id": 1892347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-19T09:06:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s slightly awkward to add `to_parent`, because it is initialized after the creation of the transaction object. Right now, the easiest way to add it would be to wrap the field in a spinlock. This is probably fine since the spinlock is entirely uncontended, but it would be nicer if we could avoid it (after all it\u0027s not necessary).\n\nThere are various ways we could avoid the spinlock. For example, we could use `LockedBy` to say that it\u0027s locked by the target process. However, because I have separate locks per thread, this is a bit annoying to do, as `LockedBy` requires you to know which spinlock to associate it with at creation.",
      "parentUuid": "1b69ee1c_f926f58b",
      "revId": "0dfd18dc7d1428993739d87d1ab015e8424b4393",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
